      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi John,\nI’ve moved the new Mapper6 APIs into gralloc5.cpp.\nAre you suggesting this approach because stable-c lacks a versioning concept, meaning any future changes would remain under gralloc5/mapper5?\nWe’re considering whether it would be cleaner to introduce a dedicated structure for the new version, such as:\n\nGralloc6.h / Gralloc6.cpp\nA Gralloc6Mapper class inheriting from Gralloc5Mapper\n\nThis would make the additions for Mapper6 explicit and maintain clarity around version-specific changes. It seems like a more maintainable and transparent solution.\nPlease share your thoughts.",
      "revId": "065752e2e4cf35fe0441f5e6e8a2a61d9b72bee8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
