      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T18:05:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Critical issue with pointer handling / type casting:\n\n`\u0026outViewList` passes the memory address of the local stack pointer parameter `outViewList`.\n1. If `mMapper-\u003ev6.getMultiViewInfo` expects `const uint32_t**` to return a pointer to an internal array, assigning into `\u0026outViewList` only overwrites the local stack argument `outViewList`, which is discarded upon return. The caller\u0027s output buffer is never populated.\n2. If `mMapper-\u003ev6.getMultiViewInfo` expects `uint32_t*` (a buffer provided by the caller to be populated), passing `\u0026outViewList` passes `uint32_t**`, causing the HAL implementation to write array elements over the stack frame, leading to stack corruption.\n\nPlease verify the C-API signature and contract of `AIMapper_v6::getMultiViewInfo` and ensure caller buffer population or pointer handling is correctly implemented.\n\n*(Generated by Jetski)*",
      "revId": "065752e2e4cf35fe0441f5e6e8a2a61d9b72bee8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
